<name>Freeze Frame Data/Detailed Diagnostic Information</name>
<subpara id="RM00000060400UX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___00004J000000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>About Freeze Frame Data Output</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>The skid control computer (built into the actuator) stores the vehicle (sensor) conditions when the system operates or when a malfunction DTC is output, and these can be displayed using the SST (TaSCAN).</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Freeze Frame Data During System Operation</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Data is stored when the system operates and is updated each time the system operates.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>The number of times the IG has been turned OFF → ON since the system last operated is stored and displayed up to 31 times.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The IG ON count is incremented only when the vehicle is driven at 7km/h or more after the IG is turned OFF → ON.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If "Number of IG ON Times Since Freeze" exceeds 31, "31" is displayed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>When freeze frame data from when a malfunction DTC occurred is stored, the freeze frame data from system operation is cleared.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Freeze Frame Data When Malfunction DTC Occurs</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>When a malfunction DTC is output, the freeze frame data from when the malfunction code occurred is stored.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Once freeze frame data from when a malfunction DTC occurred is stored, the freeze frame data is not updated until the DTCs are cleared.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>In freeze frame data from when a malfunction DTC occurred, "Number of IG ON Times Since Freeze" is not stored.</ptxt>
